POST /api/v2/folder/{folder_id}/list_template/{template_id}
Create a new list using a list template in a Folder. Publicly shared templates must be [added to your Workspace](https://help.clickup.com/hc/en-us/articles/6326023965591-Add-a-template-to-your-library) before you can use them with the public API. This request runs synchronously by default with `return_immediately=true`. The request returns the future List ID immediatly, but the List may not be created when the response is sent. Small templates can be applied synchronously, which guarantees that all sub objects are created. In case of a timeout on synchronous requests, the objects from the template will continue to be created past the timeout.
Required: folder_id (path) — ID of the Folder where the List will be created; template_id (path) — ID of the List template to use. Template IDs include a `t-` prefix (e.g., `t-15363293`). Retrieve available template IDs using the [Get List Templates](#tag/Templates/operation/GetListTemplates) endpoint.; body (body)

DELETE /api/v2/folder/{folder_id}
Delete a Folder from your Workspace.
Required: folder_id (path)

PUT /api/v2/folder/{folder_id}
Rename a Folder. Renaming a subfolder leaves it nested inside its parent Folder, and the response includes the `parent_folder` field. This endpoint only renames a Folder. To nest a Folder inside another Folder or move it to another Space, use the [Move Folder](#tag/Folders/operation/MoveFolder) endpoint; a `parent_folder_id` sent to this endpoint is ignored.
Required: folder_id (path); body (body)
